# FIL frontend (Wes Bos style)

Practical, readable React — **hooks over classes, small files, explicit types, no clever abstractions.**

## Stack

- React 19, TypeScript 5.9+, Vite 8, Vitest 4
- Vitest + Testing Library
- `@fil/app` (staff SPA), `@fil/widget` (embed)
- Path alias: `@/` → `src/`

## Folder layout

```
src/
  components/       # Presentational + container split when it helps
  hooks/            # useHealth, useGridQuery, useSession — data & UI state
  lib/api/          # fetch client + per-resource API functions
  pages/            # Route-level components (when router added)
  types/            # Shared TS types (api.ts, grid.ts)
  __tests__/        # Mirror src structure
widget/src/         # Separate IIFE bundle — keep tiny
```

## Components

- **Function components only** — no class components
- **Named exports** for components (`export function LeadGrid()`)
- One main component per file; colocate small subcomponents if <30 lines and private
- Props: define `interface LeadGridProps { … }` above the component
- Keep JSX readable — extract handlers and derived values before `return`
- When adapting legacy grids: keep AG Grid patterns; strip multisite concepts

## Hooks (custom hooks for everything reusable)

- Data fetching → `useHealth`, `useSession`, `useGridQuery`
- Wrap async in hooks; components call the hook, not raw `fetch`
- Return stable shapes: `{ data, error, isLoading, refetch }`
- `useMemo` / `useCallback` only when profiling or deps for child memoization warrant it — not by default

```tsx
// hooks/useHealth.ts
export function useHealth() {
  const [state, setState] = useState<AsyncState<HealthResponse>>({ status: 'loading' });

  useEffect(() => {
    let cancelled = false;
    fetchHealth()
      .then((data) => { if (!cancelled) setState({ status: 'success', data }); })
      .catch((error) => { if (!cancelled) setState({ status: 'error', error }); });
    return () => { cancelled = true; };
  }, []);

  return state;
}
```

When building grids: **SWR** or **useSWRMutation** — one hook per API surface.

## API layer (`lib/api/`)

- **`client.ts`** — shared `apiGet`, `apiPost`, `apiDelete`; credentials `include` for Sanctum
- Throw **`ApiError`** with `status` and body — don’t swallow failures
- **One file per resource**: `health.ts`, `session.ts`, `leads.ts`
- Types live in `types/api.ts` or next to the fetch function
- Base URL: `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL ?? '/api'`

```ts
// lib/api/client.ts pattern
export class ApiError extends Error {
  constructor(public status: number, message: string, public body?: unknown) {
    super(message);
  }
}
```

No API calls inside random components — always go through `lib/api` or hooks.

## Auth (staff app)

- **`AuthProvider`** loads `GET /api/v1/session` on boot; 401 → `/login`
- **`RequireAuth`** wraps staff routes; **`RequirePermission`** gates pages
- **`useAuth()`** / **`useCan('leads.view')`** — no hard-coded role strings
- Nav from **`user.navigation`** (server-driven); see `docs/AUTH.md`

## TypeScript

- Prefer `interface` for object shapes; `type` for unions and utilities
- Avoid `any`; use `unknown` + narrowing for catch blocks
- Use `satisfies` for config objects when useful
- Don't over-generic hooks unless reused 3+ times

## State

- Local UI state: `useState`
- Server state: hooks + SWR (stale-while-revalidate) when we port listings
- Avoid Redux/Zustand until cross-page state actually hurts
- URL state for filters/tabs when possible (shareable, bookmarkable)

## Styling (theme tokens)

FIL uses **CSS variables in `index.css`** + **Tailwind class strings in `lib/ui/tokens.ts`**. Theme switching is automatic via `[data-theme='dark']` on `<html>` — do not add per-component `dark:` overrides for semantic colors.

### Where to change things

| Need | Edit |
| ---- | ---- |
| New color that must work in light + dark | Add paired `--color-*` vars in `index.css` `@theme` + `[data-theme='dark']`, then expose a token in `tokens.ts` |
| Text link | `<TextLink>` or `textLink` / `textLinkPlain` |
| Form input | `formControl` + `formFocus` (see `FormField`) |
| Filter/chip pill | `chipActive` / `chipInactive` |
| Badge / alert | `<Badge>` / `<Alert>` (backed by `badge` / `alert` tokens) |
| Button | `<Button>` (backed by `button` tokens) |
| Tinted callout / metric card | `surface.*` helpers |
| Primary CTA color | `bg-primary`, `text-link`, `text-primary` — not raw `brand-600` |

### Do not

- Pair `bg-brand-50` with `text-brand-700` (breaks in dark mode)
- Use `text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400` — use `text-link` instead
- Use light-only Tailwind palette for status (`green-100`, `amber-100`) — use `tone-*` tokens
- Import from `lib/ui/surfaces.ts` in new code — use `lib/ui/tokens.ts`

Verify new UI in **both light and dark** before finishing.

## Testing (Vitest)

- `@testing-library/react` — test behavior, not implementation
- Mock **`lib/api`** modules or hooks, not deep fetch internals
- `findBy*` for async UI; `getByRole` over test IDs when accessible
- Run: `npm run test:run`

## Widget (`frontend/widget/`)

- Minimal IIFE; no React router
- PostMessage / `data-site-key` contract documented in OpenAPI
- Separate Vite config; output to `backend/public/widget/`

## Do not

- Vendor-specific legacy constants or proxy URLs in new code
- Fetch in `useEffect` without cleanup (cancel flag or AbortController)
- Giant `App.tsx` — split into pages as routes land
- Default exports for components (except `main.tsx` entry)
- Copy-paste ES hooks — adapt to `useGridQuery` + `/api/v1/query/*`

## Iteration gate (every chunk)

Before the next feature chunk: dedupe API hooks/components, simplify, run `npm run test:run` (and `npm run build` if routes changed). Do not add pages without tests.

Verification: `cd frontend && npm run test:run`
